  "derivations": {
    "hmf_ratio": "Use the paper scripts and released HMF bins. FOF: preserve sorted published-bin pairs and geometric mean mass coordinates. M200c: match published mass centers after the 2e8 Msun completeness cut. Ratios and asymmetric plotted bounds use the released Poisson uncertainties; no catalog rebinning.",
    "assembly": "Use median_M_msun, p16_M_msun and p84_M_msun from the paper’s Warren-corrected positive-mass histories, in the same six final-mass windows and z<=8. These are absolute masses in Msun, not medians of individual normalized histories.",
    "halfmass": "Use the paper’s zhalf column (mean individual-halo formation redshift), M0_mean_msun and halo 16/84 percentiles from the same-TrackId table.",
    "projection": "Original PNG bytes; CSS viewports select existing panels. Independent original color normalization. No generated or interpolated fields.",
    "power": "Simulation curves use original power_spectrum_measurements.csv samples selected by the paper family/snapshot mapping and k<=0.25*pi*1024/L. BT/PL uses the released ratio samples with the same limit. HMcode curves use the paper’s theory_curve aggregation of published HMcode values; simulation/HMcode uses the separate released residual bins, preserving its tabulated sim_over_hmcode values. Low-k points remain visible with the existing 4*kf indicator. No finite-volume or grid-window correction.",
    "input_ratio": "Divide input spectra on identical stored k samples only. Retain the source normalization; this is input linear matter power, not the nonlinear output or a newly normalized primordial spectrum.",
    "resolution": "Published FOF resolution/volume table. Open markers indicate mean-bin masses below 50 times that run's particle mass. Mesh convergence is the tabulated PL P_mesh512/P_mesh1024 at z=0; no new simulations.",
    "concentration_reference": "Use tabulated simulation/theory ratios. Reconstruct halo percentile bounds by dividing retained simulation percentiles by theory_c200c. The source ratio_low/high fields are not used as absolute interval endpoints.",
    "profile_ratio": "Retain released radial density ratios and intervals constructed from separate bootstrap bounds; these are not a paired bootstrap distribution of the ratio."
  },
